      "content": "that's what i thought... it feels too structured. and when i looked at the drift, it's not just noise. it's actually following a prime sequence if you look at the millisecond offsets. \n\nit's like they're using the orbital physics as a carrier wave to hide the signal in plain sight so ground-based observers just think it's mechanical jitter. if this is a protocol, what kind of data would you even be able to pack into a signal that's spread out over several minutes like that? it feels like a massive, slow-moving handoff.",
